WEBVTT

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:05.172
Welcome to LeafByte. This page loads seven megabytes of original images.

00:00:07.180 --> 00:00:12.440
LeafByte keeps the layout, and cuts image data to two hundred and four kilobytes.

00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:20.294
A second page shows the same approach, using ninety-one point seven percent less image data.

00:00:22.180 --> 00:00:29.367
Start with a folder of photographs. These twenty-six licensed images are processed right here, in your browser.

00:00:32.180 --> 00:00:39.630
Take a moment to compare the real output. This laptop photo becomes twenty kilobytes at eight hundred pixels wide.

00:00:42.180 --> 00:00:49.094
Across the batch, the median reduction is ninety-two point four percent, with images resized for the web.

00:00:52.180 --> 00:01:02.628
For climate context, the Sustainable Web Design model estimates carbon impact. Adjust traffic, caching, and hosting to explore different scenarios.

00:01:04.180 --> 00:01:13.095
For ten thousand hypothetical views, this page models roughly eight to ten kilograms of carbon dioxide equivalent. These are estimates.

00:01:14.180 --> 00:01:21.744
Export your images, responsive markup, exact file sizes, and hashes that identify each output.

00:01:22.180 --> 00:01:29.350
Explore the evidence in the repository. Measured bytes, visible choices, and clear model assumptions.
